    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0295" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg199"/>

                <head>No. 154.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward
                            Thornton to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-07-04"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 4, 1872</date>.
                        (Received July 5.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your note of yesterday, I have
                    the honor to inform you that as soon as it was announced to Her Majesty’s
                    government that the United States Government was prepared to carry out the
                    survey of <pb facs="0296" n="200" xml:id="pg200"/> the northwest boundary
                    between the Lake of the Woods and the Rocky Mountains, and that Mr. Archibald
                    Campbell was appointed as commissioner for that purpose, Captain Cameron was
                    also appointed in the same character on the part of Her Majesty’s government.
                    The preparation of the necessary instruments was at once taken in hand, and
                    Captain Cameron was instructed to proceed to Washington for the purpose of
                    putting himself in communication with Mr. Campbell, with a view to arranging the
                    plans for their future proceedings.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EDWD. THORNTON.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
